# The front door links ./mirror/*.html — the same layout the gh-pages
# projection publishes. Pages serves site/ verbatim, where the mirror lives
# under registry/mirror, so rewrite (200, not 302) to keep the URL the page
# links to.
#
# The target is the extensionless path on purpose: Pages answers any request
# for *.html with a 308 to the extensionless URL, even after a rewrite. Pointing
# the rewrite straight at /registry/mirror/<name> serves the page in one hop
# instead of two. Measured: /mirror/verify.html was 308 -> 200, and is 200 after
# this change (scripts/test-showcase-ui.mjs asserts the titles either way).
/mirror/ai.html       /registry/mirror/ai       200
/mirror/gallery.html  /registry/mirror/gallery  200
/mirror/verify.html   /registry/mirror/verify   200
